    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d138">

                <pb facs="0306" n="210" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg210"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr. Denby.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-03-21"><hi rendition="#italic">March 21,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1553.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 2861, of the 4th ultimo, inclosing a copy of a decree of the
                    Emperor of China relating to the antiforeign riots in Shantung.</p>
                <p>The provision in the decree, that “in the event of worthless and reckless fellows
                    again making trouble and committing acts of violence, the local authorities of
                    the place will be held solely responsible,” has been read with satisfaction, as
                    it affords a long-demanded guaranty for the future.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
